CrowdSec on FenrirOS
====================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled and nothing is configured. This
package is the engine (crowdsec), its Local API and cscli, plus the
notification plugins in /usr/lib/crowdsec/plugins. The firewall bouncers
(that actually block addresses) are separate packages.

1. Copy the examples you want from /usr/share/doc/crowdsec/examples into
   /etc/crowdsec (config.yaml, acquis.yaml, profiles.yaml, simulation.yaml,
   console.yaml, patterns/ ...). In acquis.yaml list the logs to watch.
2. cscli hub update; cscli collections install crowdsecurity/linux (the hub
   is downloaded from the CrowdSec hub only when you run these commands).
3. Register the local machine with its own Local API:
       cscli machines add --auto
   and, only if you want to share signals and receive the community
   blocklist, enroll with the Central API yourself: `cscli capi register`
   (nothing is sent anywhere until you do).
4. dinitctl enable crowdsec

The Local API listens on 127.0.0.1:8080 and the Prometheus metrics on
127.0.0.1:6060 in the example configuration. The example daily cron job
(crowdsec.cron.daily, hub updates) is not installed: copy it to /etc/cron.d
only if you want it.
